e in sinusitis is a known complication of undiagnosed foreign bodies\n  nasal discharge with worsening pain following decongestant use → superimposed structural complication → Structural Deformity with Secondary Infection (Septal Perforation with Granulation Tissue)\n    (frequency: rare)\n    Suggestion: Assess for septal perforation and granulation tissue via nasal endoscopy, which could explain treatment resistance in a patient with known asthma (potential steroid use history)\n\nWhen indirect_reasoning_chains are present, generate candidates that investigate the INTERMEDIATE phenotype to confirm or rule out the indirect association."}
